<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="009" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-08: Scope-check PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id} (+ H-8a comment cleanup)</title>
    <phase>0 Enforcement Remediation</phase>
    <gate>after-001</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs on an authorization path (external write endpoint) — FULL per root CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Apply the existing record∈accessible-set check pattern (already used by the sibling read path) to one write endpoint; fully specified by A-7 evidence.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches Api/ExternalAccess/** — known contended path (sibling files modified by tasks 008/010/011/016/017/018).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, endpoints, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close finding A-7 (spec FR-08, High): PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id} must scope-check the record before writing. Today the handler acknowledges in a comment that it performs no record-scope check — any resolvable external caller can modify any To Do by GUID. Verify the target To Do resolves within the caller's accessible root set before applying the update; deny otherwise. Also remove the stale comments naming the deleted ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter/ExternalCallerContext in the same file (register H-8a).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the external-access scoped-read pipeline (CallerPrincipal, AccessibleRecordSetService, ExternalModuleRegistry). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The PATCH endpoint denies (403/404) any caller whose accessible root set does not cover the target To Do; a caller with zero accessible roots can modify nothing. The write goes through the same scoping model the scoped read path already enforces.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Finding A-7 (design-register §A.1): "PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id} has no record-scope check (self-acknowledged in comment)" — evidence Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:328-345. Effect: any resolvable caller modifies any To Do by GUID. The scoped READ path shows the enforcement pattern to mirror: ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.GetScopedRecordAsync:266-273 (CallerPrincipal path + ExecuteScopedFetchAsync + ExternalModuleRegistry) — per the A-15 confirmation, this is where live Tier-2 enforcement actually runs. H-8a (design-register §H.8): stale comments at ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:13, :24, :339 name the deleted ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter / ExternalCallerContext — remove while in the file. Design §8 note: A-7 becomes a genuine vulnerability the moment To Dos become an access-scoped child module (Phase 3) — this must land in Phase 0.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalTodoScopeTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="completed">⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-24 (review finding). Task 001 did NOT author a characterization for A-7 — notes/task-001-untestable-findings.md §2(b) records the PATCH handler as unreachable offline, so there is NOTHING TO FLIP. Do not go looking for one. The only related test is the fail-closed negative PatchExternalTodo_WhenCallerCannotBeResolvedToExternalPrincipal_IsRejected in EndpointAuthorizationCharacterizationTests.cs — that is a gate that must STAY, not a characterization to invert. This task owns its own coverage.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: if the To Do cannot be read, has no resolvable root, or the accessible-set lookup errors, DENY — never apply the PATCH. Scope: the scope check added here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Root-set resolution reuses the existing CallerPrincipal/AccessibleRecordSetService composition — do not build a parallel membership query. Scope: the lookup mechanism chosen.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Prefer expressing the check as an endpoint filter consistent with the route group's pattern; inline service-call acceptable only if the sibling scoped routes do the same — match the file's live convention. Scope: the PATCH route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Respond 404 (not 403) when hiding record existence is the established convention on the external plane — match what the scoped read path returns for out-of-scope records. Scope: the deny response shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF-touching task (CLAUDE.md §10): report publish size vs ~44.96 MB baseline in PR; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06). Scope: this task's PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-001">OWN-COVERAGE OBLIGATION — omitted when the other seven were filed, corrected 2026-08-24 by the review. A-7 was NOT pinned by task 001 (the PATCH handler is unreachable offline behind CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter), so this task owns its coverage entirely. Tests go at tests/integration/auth/** (the ADR-038 KEEP path). Extract a seam if needed rather than mocking transport.</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">LESSON THAT APPLIES DIRECTLY HERE. Mocking at a seam proves the CALLER handles a failure, never that the CALLEE reports one. The review found four load-bearing methods in this project executed by NO test, each with a one-line perturbation that fails zero tests -- including the central delegation probe. When you add the scope check, perturb it (invert the in-scope test, make the accessible-set resolver return everything) and record how many tests fail. A perturbation that fails ZERO means the test is at the wrong level: fix the test, do not drop the perturbation. Rationale: notes/review-2026-08-24-findings.md section 3.</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">DO NOT TOUCH tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/ExternalScopeCharacterizationTests.cs -- the path this POML originally named. It does not exist at that location, and the file of that name at tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ belongs to A-17 / pending task 011. Editing it would collide with 011 on a parallel-unsafe surface.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>external plane record scoping</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization-seams.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/10-finding-confirmations.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="endpoint-filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Filter attachment pattern</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare FULL rigor.</step>
    <step order="1">Read ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:300-360 and the scoped-read enforcement at ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs:266-273; determine how the To Do's root (project) is resolved on the read side.</step>
    <step order="2">Before the update: read the target To Do's root lookup, resolve the caller's accessible set for that root entity, and deny (matching the read path's out-of-scope response) when the root is not in the set.</step>
    <step order="3">Restrict the PATCH surface to the fields the endpoint intends to update (no open property bag pass-through) — verify current behavior and pin it.</step>
    <step order="4">Delete the stale H-8a comments at :13, :24, :339.</step>
    <step order="5">Author the coverage yourself at tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalTodoScopeTests.cs — there is NO task-001 characterization to flip (see the corrected dependency note). Cover: an in-scope To Do PATCHes successfully; an out-of-scope To Do is denied; a zero-root caller is denied; a nonexistent To Do does not disclose existence. Do NOT weaken PatchExternalTodo_WhenCallerCannotBeResolvedToExternalPrincipal_IsRejected — it is the fail-closed gate this task strengthens. Mock at the virtual seam; Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; stays banned (ADR-038 B1).</step>
    <step order="6">Run full test suite; build green.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document response-shape choice (403 vs 404) in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the To Do's root cannot be resolved through an existing accessible-set entity (A-9: only 3 root sets exist — project/matter/WA), STOP and escalate: scoping to "todo regarding project only" vs denying todos with other parents is a product decision, not an implementation detail.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ — the ADR-038 security-auth KEEP path this
    project has used for every task's coverage. No existing file covers the external To Do PATCH scope
    check; task 001 could not reach the handler offline, which is why A-7 was never pinned.</existing>
    <extension>A new test file inside the existing KEEP path, not a new production component. It cannot
    extend ExternalScopeCharacterizationTests: that file is A-17's FetchXml suite and belongs to pending
    task 011, and editing it would collide on a parallel-unsafe surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it the PATCH scope check ships unverified, and the review of 2026-08-24
    established that this project has four load-bearing methods executed by no test — each with a one-line
    perturbation that fails zero tests. An unverified authorization check on a mutation is exactly that
    shape: it can be silently inverted with no signal.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/ExternalScopeCharacterizationTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller with zero accessible roots cannot modify a To Do by GUID — the PATCH is denied (FR-08 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller whose accessible set covers the To Do's root can still PATCH it (no over-denial).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a To Do whose root is OUTSIDE the caller's accessible set is denied with the same response shape the scoped read path uses for out-of-scope records.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a nonexistent To Do id denies (404), never errors unhandled.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The stale ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter/ExternalCallerContext comments (:13, :24, :339) are removed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; build green; publish size reported in PR and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-08; finding A-7; H-8a rider. Phase 3 will make sprk_todo a scoped child module — this fix is the Phase 0 stopgap on the write path; keep the mechanism aligned with the read path so Phase 3 can subsume it.</notes>

  <completion date="2026-08-24">
    <summary>FR-08 / A-7 closed. The PATCH handler now resolves the to-do's regarding-project via the
    new ExternalDataService.GetTodoProjectAsync (mirroring task 027's GetDocumentProjectAndNameAsync)
    and denies unless the root is in the caller's accessible set AND the caller holds Write. ADR-003
    fail-closed on absent / unreadable / no-resolvable-root. H-8a stale comments corrected in this file.</summary>
    <escalation-fired>YES — the regarding-scope trigger. sprk_todo has 13 regarding-parent lookups
    (live metadata; the code said 11) and only 3 map to a CallerPrincipal accessible set. Shipped
    project-only + deny-the-rest, which keeps the write surface exactly as wide as the project-scoped
    read surface. Whether matter / work-assignment parents should be PATCHable is an OPEN OWNER
    DECISION — see notes/task-009-external-todo-scope.md.</escalation-fired>
    <coverage>tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalTodoScopeTests.cs — 9 tests.
    Perturbations: remove HasProjectAccess 1 fail · remove Write-rights 1 fail · write-before-check
    8 fails · drop 404 guard 1 fail. The FIRST perturbation initially failed ZERO (the rights check
    redundantly denies out-of-scope); fixed by asserting WHICH guard denied, per the review constraint.</coverage>
    <gates>11,383 passed / 0 failed across all 7 projects · --warnaserror clean · publish 43.70 MB
    compressed incl PDBs (ceiling 60, baseline 43.69) · no vulnerable packages</gates>
    <notes-doc>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-009-external-todo-scope.md</notes-doc>
  </completion>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
